   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, the derivative of the integral with respect to its upper limit is the integrand evaluated at that limit, \\( \\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Ln",
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The upper limit is \\( x^{3} \\), so the chain rule multiplies by its derivative: \\( g'(x) = \\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)} \\cdot 3 x^{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            3,
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               2
            ],
            [
               "Ln",
               [
                  "Power",
                  "x",
                  3
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( x = 2 \\) the limit is \\( 8 \\) and its derivative is \\( 12 \\).",
         "mathjson": 12
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( g'\\left(2\\right) = 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\cdot 12 = 36 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
